Expected elements: present

No MUST NOT SHOW item appears, and the DATA row is the transaction pane's first labelled row, correctly toned. Position is unmistakable at code line 32 and the ACIR column is properly tabular; the weakness is several typographic systems running in parallel where one should.

Round changes. (a) Landed, and better than asked: the fade runs on both axes — the Code pane fades line 52 at its foot and fades long lines out at its right edge (lines 40, 48, 49) — and is correctly absent from Call Trace and Values, where content genuinely ends, so it reads as signal, not decoration. My last-round "tail cut mid-line at y897" was wrong and is withdrawn. The proportion complaint stands on its own merits: DATA plus its four sentences still occupy y218-452, ~234px of the pane's 820px (~28%), unchanged, and the fade makes that cost more legible, not less. (b) Landed; side effect — "Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded", three rows above, is now the only machine-shaped string left in the pane. (c) Capitalisation landed; the terminator sits under the fade and is not verifiable at this height. (d) Not verifiable — no Selector or Raw row is on screen at laptop height.

Highest-priority fixes: one numeric convention (the call trace groups thousands, COST - MANA does not), and one hash strategy (the pane truncates its own hash then prints it in full directly beneath, while addresses wrap to two-character orphans "32" and "4c").

Rating: 6/10

